      "part_type": "Hadith",
      "path": "/books/al-kafi:6:2:74:16",
      "text": [
        " لَا يَكُونُ اللِّعَانُ إِلَّا بِنَفْيِ وَلَدٍ وَ قَالَ إِذَا قَذَفَ الرَّجُلُ امْرَأَتَهُ لَاعَنَهَا ."
      ],
      "translations": {
        "en.hubeali": [
          "Muhammad Bin Yahya, from Ahmad Bin Muhammad, from Ali Bin Hadeed, from Jameel Bin Darraj, from Muhammad Bin Muslim, ",
          "(It has been narrated) from one of the two (5th or the 6th Imam<sup>asws</sup>) having said: ‘The cursing does not happen except by the denial of a child’. And he<sup>asws</sup> said: ‘When the man slanders his wife, he would curse her’."
        ],
        "en.sarwar": [
          "16. Muhammad ibn Yahya has narrated from Ahmad ibn Muhammad, from Ali ibn Hadid from Jamil ibn Darraj from Muhammad ibn Muslim who has said the following: “One of the two Imam, (abu Ja‘far or abu ‘Abd Allah), Alayhim al-Salam, has said, ‘al-Li‘an (condemnation) does not take place without denying the child.’ He (the Imam) said, ‘When a man accuses his woman he can go through the process of al-Li‘an (condemnation) against her.’” "
        ]
      }
    },
